  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation of Enhanced Efficiency Fertilisers: Exploring Next-Gen Fertilisers for Smallholders in Sub-Saharan Africa.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, led by the International Fertiliser Development Centre (IFDC), will conduct a comprehensive evaluation of Enhanced Efficiency Fertilisers (EEFs) with a focus on sub-Saharan Africa (SSA). The evaluation will benchmark these innovative products against urea, conduct greenhouse evaluations in two contrasting soil types (specifically in soil pH), and carry out field evaluations for different crops and soils in SSA. In addition, the project will further evaluate a selected set of EEFs, chosen based on their performance in laboratory and greenhouse evaluations, through on-farm field trials in two sub-Saharan African (SSA) countries (Tanzania and Zambia). It will also leverage the on-going trials conducted by the USAID-funded IFDC Space to Place Project on improving fertilizer use efficiency in SSA. For example, the Space to Place trials will provide the balanced fertilization requirements for P, K, and secondary and micronutrients thereby ensuring the N response and NUE is not limited by other nutrients. The specific objectives are as follows:

a) Systematic screening of enhanced efficiency nitrogen fertilizers for their nutrient release patterns, transformations, volatilization losses, leaching and nitrous oxide emissions.

b) Screening and field evaluation of enhanced efficiency nitrogen fertilizers for their impact on growth and productivity for various crops on different soils.

c) Development and validation of a Decision Support Tool (DST) for Enhanced Efficiency Nitrogen Fertilizers in Sub-Saharan Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
